  "_commit": {
    "id": "171c1a2cfbd1e679a6f5ded77a1747c3d525a743",
    "author": "tgirke <tgirke@citrus.ucr.edu>",
    "committer": "tgirke <tgirke@citrus.ucr.edu>",
    "message": "Extend TTD parser with cross-reference, UniProt, indication and\nmolecule-type columns; fix cold-cache bugs; add fields= support\n\n- buildTtdDb()/ttdTargetAnnot(): add PubChem_CID/SID, CAS, ChEBI_ID\n  (TTD's cross-matching file); Uniprot_acc + uniprot_source (resolved\n  via the package's UniProt REST scaffold, keyed on GeneName, with\n  TTD_missing/unresolved/resolved/resolution_failed provenance);\n  molecule_type (TTD's own DRUGTYPE field primarily, SMILES/name\n  heuristic fallback for the ~30% of drugs without one); Indication\n  (per-drug, per-disease clinical status, packed from P1-05, richer\n  than the single Highest_status). Normalizes MOA's literal \".\"\n  sentinel to NA. Records each source file's own (version, date) in a\n  new ttd_release table, exposed as attr(result, \"ttd_release\").\n- .getCacheFile()/downloadTTD(): raise a clear error on a cold\n  BiocFileCache lookup instead of silently propagating NA into a\n  cryptic file() error downstream.\n- ttdTargetAnnot()/broadRepurposingHubAnnot()/gtoPdbTargetAnnot(): add\n  fields = \"core\"/\"all\"/<vector> support (mirroring the four\n  REST-backed sources) and register all three in\n  listDrugTargetFields(); queryDrugTargets() now forwards ... to them\n  too.\n- Vignette: fix rerun = FALSE -> TRUE on the first build for\n  TTD/Broad/GtoPdb (was a hard failure on a cold cache); update the\n  TTD section to demonstrate the new columns, fields=, and\n  attr(result, \"ttd_release\").\n",
    "time": 1784601766
  },
